# CODEOWNERS for clearmeasure-aisf-sample-apps/basic-environment-octopus-codefresh
# (staged at platform/CODEOWNERS in the app checkout; see design §6.2).
#
# The branch ruleset on `main` requires a pull request, code-owner approval and
# the `codefresh/env-checks` status. Its bypass list holds only team
# `platform-bots` (the Octopus Git credential's machine user), which may commit
# `images[].newTag` in gitops/workorders/envs/*/kustomization.yaml and nothing
# else. `scripts/checks/tool-boundaries.sh --audit-bot-commits` enforces that.
#
# `<org>` is a placeholder for the GitHub organization. Replace the two team
# placeholders when the repo is attached (R1). The last matching pattern wins.
# When a line lists two teams, an approval from either team satisfies it.

# Default: every path has an owner, so the code-owner requirement always applies.
*                                   @<org>/platform-owners

# This file.
/CODEOWNERS                         @<org>/platform-owners

# Shared Kustomize base: a merged change reaches tdd, uat and prod at once.
# Pull requests that change runtime behaviour here also need the
# `all-environments` label (ADR-D6). Roll-through changes go in components/.
/gitops/workorders/base/            @<org>/platform-owners

# Environment pins. Octopus writes `newTag` directly (ruleset bypass);
# a human pull request here is a break-glass change (docs/runbooks/break-glass.md).
/gitops/workorders/envs/*/kustomization.yaml    @<org>/platform-owners

# Argo CD bootstrap, cluster roots, AppProjects, add-ons and Applications.
/argocd/                            @<org>/platform-owners

# Admission and Octopus policies. §6.2 names platform owners; §6.1 marks the
# tree as security-owned. Both teams are listed until the chief architect
# settles which one alone approves (docs/consistency-notes.md).
/policies/                          @<org>/platform-owners @<org>/security-owners

# Privileged Azure foundation: every role assignment, lock and policy (ADR-D10).
/terraform/foundation/              @<org>/security-owners

# Secret-scanning configuration.
/.gitleaks.toml                     @<org>/security-owners
